body: "## Scope and documented goal\nFound on PR #122 head cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83; this is a source-backed defect in the proposed opt-in conflict implementation, not a claim about the released version.\n\n[ARCHITECTURE.md](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83/ARCHITECTURE.md#L659-L671) says structural disagreements require explicit reconciliation and are never silently recorded as resolved. The [canonical feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83/.agents/pm/features/pm-vcs-p7objects.toon) requires durable alternatives and preserved independent edits.\n\n## Defect and impact\nThe [new refusal predicate](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83/engine/repo.ts#L2015-L2017) accepts a reported conflict whenever its resulting path has any conflict IDs. It does not establish that those IDs represent this disagreement.\n\n[mergeTrees](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83/engine/rewrite.ts#L330-L356) retains our entry for delete/edit and mode disagreements. If that entry already contains an unresolved field/text unit, the predicate accepts the old metadata. The subsequent [commit/HEAD publication](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83/engine/repo.ts#L2040-L2050) has no structural-disagreement representation. Resolving the older unit can therefore remove the remaining durable signal while the deletion or mode choice was never reconciled.\n\n## Sanitized reproduction and observed result\nExecuted the exact pinned mergeTrees function with in-memory tree adapters, followed by the exact refusal predicate:\n- Base: path f, payload base, mode 100644, stable file identity\n- Ours: payload ours, mode 100644, with an existing unresolved unit\n- Theirs: path absent; separately, payload theirs and mode 100755\n- Both sides differ from base\n\nActual: mergeTrees reports content/mode conflicts, preserves the existing unit, and the new structural-refusal predicate evaluates false in both cases.\nExpected: unsupported_recorded_conflict before publishing the merge.\n\nNegative controls removing the existing unit make the predicate correctly evaluate true in both cases.\n\n## Method and limits\nThe merge function and predicate were executed unchanged with in-memory I/O adapters; commit publication consequences are established by the linked call path, not by a full Repository integration run. No production repository was changed. An end-to-end branch scenario remains to be added.\n\n## Acceptance/regression criteria\n- Full Repository.merge tests for delete/edit and mode conflicts where ours already carries a recorded field or hunk unit\n- With recordConflicts enabled, refuse unsupported structural disagreements regardless of unrelated existing units; HEAD/index/worktree remain unchanged\n- Retain the current ordinary field/hunk recording behavior and the no-existing-unit negative controls\n\nAll-status issues (122 entries across two REST pages), current PR discussions/reviews, and the canonical feature were checked. Closed #26 concerns older default marker/fail-on-conflict behavior and is distinct.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T08:03:41Z)\n>\n> Addressed in PR #122 at fc0cbd022d66afc0622a224a8b2da58a75745f78; its body now contains Fixes #123. The per-disagreement recorded guard introduced in e56d356 is protected by full Repository.merge regressions through real branch edits, deletion and chmod/stage/commit operations. Test: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^structural delete\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts. All 12 field/text, inherited/clean, incoming-delete/local-delete/mode scenarios pass, and refusal preserves HEAD/index/disk/mode/merge-state/operations. Reverting only the predicate to the defective path-has-any-units check makes all four inherited field/text incoming-delete and mode cases fail; eight child controls pass (aggregate 8 pass / 5 fail including the failed parent). Both complete release gates pass 1607/1607 with all 66 source files at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. The issue remains open for review.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T11:01:13Z)\n>\n> Review-round verification on 2e85d73b106556426d158dcf1a881be2cf3afc17: the per-disagreement structural refusal and its 12 real Repository branch scenarios still pass, covering field/text inherited units, delete/edit in both directions and executable-mode changes. `node --test --test-name-pattern=\"structural delete\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts` is included in both passing full release gates (1,612/1,612 each, all 66 source files at 100% in all four coverage dimensions). The original behavioral revert remains recorded in pm-vcs-p7objects and the PR body; `Fixes #123` is retained in the PR body. Internal preflight status reads now also preserve aged cold indexes on refusal."
